# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# `go build ./...` inside an example writes a binary named after its
# directory. Those are extensionless, so none of the patterns above match
# them, and five had been committed. Two of them — examples/http/http and
# examples/composition/composition — are inside the root module, so they
# shipped in the module zip: 13 MB of a 16 MB download, on every `go get`.
examples/*/*
!examples/*/*.go
!examples/*/*.md
!examples/*/go.mod
!examples/*/go.sum
!examples/*/*.yaml
!examples/*/*.yml
!examples/*/*.json
!examples/*/Dockerfile
!examples/*/Makefile
!examples/*/*/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool
*.out
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Dependency directories
vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work

# IDE specific files
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Local configuration
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# OS specific files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/

# Build artifacts
bin/
dist/

# Profiling outputs
*.prof

# Relicta runtime state
.relicta/

# Roady runtime state (spec is materialised into docs/backlog.md and committed there)
.roady/

# Generated reports
SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT.md

# Security scanner outputs
*.sarif
nox-out/
verdict-results.*
.nox/cache/
# MkDocs staged copies of root markdown
docs/GOVERNANCE.md
docs/ADOPTERS.md
docs/SECURITY.md
docs/CHANGELOG.md
